      "question": "Relations",
      "preferredVariantId": "v-4529b70fc8",
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "v-4529b70fc8",
          "answer": "Forms medial ankle mortise and articulates with talus. Behind it run tibialis posterior, flexor digitorum longus, posterior tibial vessels, tibial nerve and flexor hallucis longus, from anterior to posterior.",
          "sources": [
            {
              "modelId": "lower-limb-model-ns10",
              "cardId": "lower-limb-model-ns10-603",
              "sourceLine": 603
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f-b03737e3cd",
      "question": "Clinical relevance",
      "preferredVariantId": "v-1b229e19da",
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "v-1b229e19da",
          "answer": "Fracture may accompany ankle instability; posterior tibial pulse lies behind it and tibial nerve can be compressed in tarsal tunnel.",
          "sources": [
